# oracle: fix filter/corotate m 1.0 (the clusters of hydrogen atoms: 19 of two atoms, 3 of four, 646 angle clusters) on the solvated peptide of examples/PACKAGES/filter_corotate/in.respa (2004 atoms), cut down for time: lj/charmm/coul/charmm 8 10 without kspace, run_style respa 2 4 with bonds and angles on level 1, the dihedrals and the pair on level 2 (the filtered level), fix nvt, 6 outer steps of 4 fs
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.3e-14, atoms 3.9e-11. The 1e-11 grows from rounding over the steps: on the full in.respa setup (pppm on level 3) the filtered and the unfiltered runs both agreed to 1e-11 after 2 steps (1.8e-11 and 1.4e-11).
# oracle-examples: PACKAGES/filter_corotate/data.peptide
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      full
pair_style      lj/charmm/coul/charmm 8.0 10.0
bond_style      harmonic
angle_style     charmm
dihedral_style  charmm
improper_style  harmonic
read_data       data.peptide
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    delay 5
thermo          2
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal ebond eangle edihed evdwl ecoul press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
timestep        4
run_style respa 2 4 bond 1 angle 1 dihedral 2 pair 2
fix             1 all nvt temp 250.0 250.0 100.0 tchain 1
fix             cor all filter/corotate m 1.0
run             6
